meta {
  name: Speaker Workflow - Slot Capacity 409
  type: http
  seq: 53
}

put {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/events/{{slotCapacityEventCode}}/speakers/{{slotCapacityCandidateSpeakerId}}/status
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{authToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "newStatus": "INVITED",
    "reason": "Story 11.B.2 - slot capacity gate contract test"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 409
  res.body.error: eq Conflict
  res.body.details.code: eq SLOT_CAPACITY_REACHED
}

tests {
  test("returns HTTP 409 when slot capacity reached on READY -> INVITED", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(409);
  });

  test("structured details surface acceptedCount, invitedCount, maxSlots (Story 11.B.2 AC4)", function() {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.details).to.be.an('object');
    expect(body.details.code).to.equal("SLOT_CAPACITY_REACHED");
    expect(body.details.acceptedCount).to.be.a('number');
    expect(body.details.invitedCount).to.be.a('number');
    expect(body.details.maxSlots).to.be.a('number');
  });

  test("includes a human-readable message", function() {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body.message).to.include("Slot capacity reached");
  });
}

docs {
  Contract test for Story 11.B.2 AC4 + Task 8.4(c) (ADR-009 §0.7 slot-capacity gate replacing
  removed OVERFLOW state).

  Setup expectation: by the time this test runs, the event referenced by
  `slotCapacityEventCode` has `count(ACCEPTED) + count(INVITED) >= max_slots`, and
  `slotCapacityCandidateSpeakerId` is a speaker pool entry at READY. The seed for the
  scenario lives in a dedicated setup `.bru` (or fixture script) that the CI runner invokes
  before this test.

  Frontend integration of the 409 surfacing UX is owned by Story 11.D.3 (kanban
  column-header "slot capacity reached" tooltip). For 11.B.2 the 409 is just a clean error
  code returned to the existing organizer Kanban flow — the UI shows whatever its current
  4xx handler renders (a generic toast) until 11.D.3 lands.

  ---
  PR 11 audit (disabled 2026-05-26): seed for this test never landed. To trigger the gate
  at the new READY → INVITED transition for an EVENING event (max_slots=4), the run would
  need: create dedicated event + add 5 speakers to pool + transition each to CONTACTED +
  promote each to READY (5 × POST /promote provisioning 5 CUMS users) + transition 4 of
  them to INVITED. ~25 setup requests / ~200 LOC of Bruno glue — blows PR 11's ~230 LOC
  budget by itself.

  Canonical coverage already exists at the integration test layer:
  SpeakerInvitationControllerIntegrationTest#should_return409_when_sendInvitationCalledAndSlotCapacityReached
  + SpeakerWorkflowServiceTest#enforceSlotCapacity_throws_when_acceptedPlusInvitedEqualsMax.
  Re-enabling this Bruno layer is a follow-up if/when the seed becomes affordable
  (e.g., a dedicated `/admin/test-fixtures/ems/seed-slot-capacity` fixture endpoint).
}
